{
  "_source": "rsprox capture local 1002310 (rev 243): each line's chathead (npc id, 0 = the player) and chat animation as live sent them (if_setnpchead/if_setplayerhead and if_setanim on chat_left/chat_right). Keyed by '<speaker name>|<text>' ('player|<text>' for the player).",
  "lines": {
    "Amascut|Adventurer, kill these pathetic priests.": [11591, 567],
    "Amascut|Have fun...": [11591, 13963],
    "Amascut|Shame. Not to worry though, I have plenty more.": [11591, 567],
    "Amascut|You! Priest of the dog lord. You are now mine. Kill your brethren!": [11591, 615],
    "Carpenter|Ah yes, it needs to be made from willow. Thing is, there's a small problem with that.": [4203, 589],
    "Carpenter|Hello, adventurer. The High Priest says that you're here to help us.": [4203, 589],
    "Carpenter|Hello. Have you given the symbol to the High Priest yet?": [4203, 589],
    "Carpenter|I imagine the High Priest will be down in the pyramid by now. You should take that to him as soon as possible.": [4203, 589],
    "Carpenter|Thank you. Now, just give me a moment...": [4203, 588],
    "Carpenter|There we go. All done.": [4203, 588],
    "Carpenter|Well you should do so as soon as possible. He'll be down in the pyramid by now.": [4203, 589],
    "Carpenter|Wow, you're quick. I'm all out of willow, and due to the quarantine, I'm unable to leave the city to get more. However, the High Priest mentioned that a special exception has been made for you.": [4203, 591],
    "Cat|Can we go to Varrock sewers and chase some rats?": [1620, 588],
    "Cat|Good, but could we go hunting again soon? One of my friends got a medal from Gertrude for catching lots of mice.": [1620, 590],
    "Cat|Hiss!": [1620, 614],
    "Cat|I want to go chase things, kill them, and then eat them, purrr.": [1620, 589],
    "Cat|I'm not too old, and not too young. In fact, I think I'm just right.": [1620, 589],
    "Cat|Me! Me! Scratch me behind the ears.": [1620, 567],
    "Cat|Meeeow.": [1620, 567],
    "Cat|Meow!": [1620, 610],
    "Cat|Meow.": [1620, 588],
    "Embalmer|Finally, I need some linen. That one shouldn't be too hard. The local cloth salesman should have some.": [4202, 589],
    "Embalmer|First, I need some salt. Normally I get mine from the salt lake just north of the city. Just fill a bucket from the lake and then use the suntrap outside to separate the salt from the water.": [4202, 591],
    "Embalmer|Hello again. Do you need something?": [4202, 554],
    "Embalmer|Next, I need some tree sap. You can use a knife to extract some from a tree, but make sure you have a bucket ready. Most coniferous evergreen trees should have some. They're the cone-shaped ones.": [4202, 591],
    "Embalmer|Oh, it's you. Any luck obtaining those items?": [4202, 554],
    "Embalmer|Oh, it's you. I hear you're helping us now. To be honest, I'm still not thrilled to have you around, but so be it.": [4202, 590],
    "Embalmer|Oh, it's you. You've already gathered everything I need. I'm sure you have plenty of other things to be doing.": [4202, 590],
    "Embalmer|Thank you. I think that's everything I need.": [4202, 588],
    "Embalmer|That's right. I need three things, but the quarantine is making some of them hard to obtain.": [4202, 589],
    "Embalmer|The local cloth salesman should have some for sale.": [4202, 588],
    "Embalmer|Well I'm afraid I can't stop to talk right now. Lots to do.": [4202, 589],
    "Embalmer|Well that was unexpected. Thank you.": [4202, 588],
    "Embalmer|Well you'd better get a move on.": [4202, 588],
    "High Priest|Ah there you are. Do you have the holy symbol?": [11649, 567],
    "High Priest|Ah, there you are. You were gone for quite a while. As a thank you for what you've done, I have a little trinket for you. I'm sure you'll get a huge amount of enjoyment out of it.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|As with many of our tombs, the pyramid has magical seals to protect it from the Devourer, the goddess of destruction. The fact that you were able to get in before means that you must have a cat.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|Besides, thanks to the plagues, we're not allowing people to leave the city. However, as you seem to be unaffected, I've told the guards to make an exception for you.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|Cats act as guardians against the Devourer. I'm surprised the Sphinx didn't tell you this. As such, only a cat can open the pyramid door.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|Did you forget that this is all your fault?": [6192, 554],
    "High Priest|For a time, Icthlarin and Amascut worked together in harmony. Icthlarin would ensure most souls are safely guided to the next life, while Amascut would select a small number to be reborn.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|For all we know, the plagues we already have could be punishment for your grave robbing!": [6192, 615],
    "High Priest|Good. Now, this ceremony is very dangerous, so we must ensure everything is done correctly.": [6192, 555],
    "High Priest|Have you helped the embalmer and the carpenter yet?": [6192, 554],
    "High Priest|Have you managed to return the jar yet?": [6192, 554],
    "High Priest|Have you not noticed the plagues already filling our city? How long before Klenter calls upon Icthlarin to send a few more?": [6192, 616],
    "High Priest|Hello again. We have a few things to finish here, but then we'll head back up into the city. Please join us there.": [11649, 590],
    "High Priest|Here in Sophanem, we support Icthlarin in his role by making sure the dead are suitably prepared for their journey.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|However, that may well be for the best. Without trade from other settlements, we've been struggling to even feed the few of us left in the city.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|Hypnotised?": [6192, 575],
    "High Priest|I didn't want to, but the other priests insisted. We had to stop the plagues from spreading. It seems that our choice was the right one. So far, the plagues have remained contained, but at a great cost.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|I don't know... Icthlarin is a patient and forgiving god. It does not make sense to me that he would do this to us.": [6192, 612],
    "High Priest|I don't think so... No wait! There is something important.": [6192, 576],
    "High Priest|I see. Fair enough.": [6192, 588],
    "High Priest|Icthlarin is the son of Tumeken and Elidinis and brother to the Devourer. He is the Menaphite god of the dead. He is responsible for ensuring the safe passage of all souls from this life to the next.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|It can't be... It's the Devourer!": [11649, 571],
    "High Priest|It does indeed. The decision to lock things down was made very quickly, so we were forced to trap many of our citizens outside the walls. We'll be able to let them all back in now.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|It is, but there is a problem.": [6192, 588],
    "High Priest|Long ago, back when Tumeken and Elidinis still walked these lands, they had two children. Icthlarin, god of the dead, was one. The other was Amascut, the goddess of rebirth.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|Luckily for us, some of her former priestesses were able to weaken her, but she still poses a great threat.": [6192, 589],
    "High Priest|Many of our citizens are trapped outside the city. Some are stuck in Menaphos, with more in other parts of the desert.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|No, just my authority. Don't forget that to enter the pyramid, you'll need a cat.": [6192, 611],
    "High Priest|No. While Icthlarin is only worshipped here, his responsibilities stretch across all of Gielinor. He cares not for an individual's beliefs. All who pass on, enter his care.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|Not great. However, we do have one bit of good news in that area, thanks to you.": [6192, 589],
    "High Priest|Not long. We need to find a way to stop the plagues soon.": [6192, 611],
    "High Priest|Not to mention, it wasn't just any jar you took. You stole a jar from the tomb of our former High Priest! Why do you think his ghost is now wandering the city once more?": [6192, 557],
    "High Priest|Now, we made many of the preparations while you were gone, but the carpenter and the embalmer could both use a hand. Could you go and speak with them?": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|Oh, er... I suppose the burial jar you took must be returned as soon as possible. That will allow my predecessor to rest once more.": [6192, 577],
    "High Priest|Once it became clear how bad it was, Menaphos, our neighbouring city, closed their gates to us and everyone else. We closed our own gates soon after.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|Perhaps Icthlarin foresaw what would happen and sent the plagues as a pre-emptive punishment?": [6192, 615],
    "High Priest|Perhaps. Either way, that jar needs to be returned.": [6192, 610],
    "High Priest|Please hurry. The people are begining to... well...": [6192, 610],
    "High Priest|Protect us, adventurer! We must complete the ceremony!": [11649, 572],
    "High Priest|Right! Of course I did. Well for us to properly reconsecrate the tomb, we must first remove those seals. That means that once we begin, the pyramid will be vulnerable until the ceremony is complete.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|She wanted to kill us all in one go?": [11649, 554],
    "High Priest|Since then, her only goal has been to devour every soul in existence, both living and dead.": [6192, 589],
    "High Priest|So what do you want from me, thief?": [6192, 554],
    "High Priest|Sorry, with all this plague business, it must have slipped my mind.": [6192, 576],
    "High Priest|Thank you so much, adventurer. Thanks to you, we were able to complete the ceremony.": [11649, 568],
    "High Priest|Thank you. We wouldn't have been able to complete the ceremony without that in our presence.": [11649, 589],
    "High Priest|That's right. We need the carpenter to create a new holy symbol for the ceremony. He lives over to the east. The embalmer also needs help gathering some supplies. He lives just south of here.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|The Sphinx? Is it possible? That contrary old cat has never done anything to help us. Prove it!": [6192, 576],
    "High Priest|The ceremony to reconsecrate Klenter's tomb of course!": [6192, 576],
    "High Priest|The embalmer lives just south of here and the carpenter lives over to the east. Please hurry. We need to get this ceremony performed before some other bad thing happens.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|The job will be done when Klenter is at rest once more.": [6192, 589],
    "High Priest|They started a few days ago. We have locusts in the east of the city and frogs in the west. The cows have started to produce sour milk, and all of us have become infected with some sort of pox.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|This is all a disaster! The plagues were bad enough, but now we've got hypnotised adventurers plundering tombs! I've only just started this job as well!": [6192, 612],
    "High Priest|Unfortunately so. Most gods have long since left this world. However, the Devourer was able to find a way to remain.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|We fear they are a punishment sent by the gods. Perhaps we have displeased Icthlarin in some way. Maybe I am to blame. All this only started after I became High Priest.": [6192, 613],
    "High Priest|We have a few things to finish here, but then we'll head back up into the city. Please join us there.": [11649, 589],
    "High Priest|We here have a lot of respect for the Sphinx. However, you should be careful of her words. She does not know the gods like we priests do.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|Well if you want to try running a city with multiple plagues, you're welcome to take over.": [6192, 615],
    "High Priest|Well now that we've sorted out this business with Klenter, we can properly focus on dealing with these plagues.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|Well on that note, what exactly did happen there? That was the Devourer!": [11649, 555],
    "High Priest|Well once again, thank you. Without you, the Devourer would have struck a devastating blow against Icthlarin.": [11649, 568],
    "High Priest|Well the pyramid has these magical seals on it...": [6192, 588],
    "High Priest|Well this is... unexpected...": [6192, 575],
    "High Priest|Well those jars are a key part of our burial practices. To remove one is to directly insult not just Icthlarin, but all those that have passed on to the next life.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|Well you could have fooled me! Good people don't rob from the dead!": [6192, 615],
    "High Priest|Well... no. While he is able to walk among us if he desires, he chooses not to so as to respect our way of life. Not to mention, his role requires his constant attention.": [6192, 578],
    "High Priest|What the...": [11649, 571],
    "High Priest|What? But we've already started.": [11649, 575],
    "High Priest|When the plagues first started, Menaphos, our neighbouring city, closed their gates as well. Many of our citizens became trapped there when they did.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|Which they are welcome to. It does not change the facts.": [6192, 589],
    "High Priest|While most of the gods, Tumeken and Elidinis included, may be long gone from Gielinor, Icthlarin remains. His important role in caring for the dead means that he is still able to interact with us.": [6192, 591],
    "High Priest|Wonderful! Now we can prepare for the ceremony.": [6192, 567],
    "High Priest|Yes. During a great war over these lands, Amascut became corrupted. She was warped into the Devourer, becoming the goddess of destruction.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|Yes. You've shown us that the pox we're all infected with can't be contagious. If it was, you'd be covered in spots by now.": [6192, 590],
    "High Priest|You! I will have no dealings with those who plunder the houses of the dead.": [6192, 615],
    "High Priest|You'd really be willing to help us again?": [6192, 554],
    "High Priest|You'd think so, but they believe there is still a danger. It seems they're even willing to kill if it helps keep their city isolated.": [6192, 616],
    "Icthlarin|Amascut! Release your hold on this human!": [4199, 614],
    "Icthlarin|And what do we have here?": [4199, 554],
    "Icthlarin|Did my sister really think that I would not sense her presence here?": [4199, 555],
    "Jex|Hey! You don't have permission to go down there.": [3875, 614],
    "Klenter|Evil doer!": [948, 614],
    "Klenter|Grave defiler!": [948, 614],
    "Klenter|Grave robber!": [948, 614],
    "Klenter|Spawn of evil!": [948, 614],
    "Klenter|Thank you, adventurer. You have given my soul some respite.": [948, 589],
    "Klenter|Thief!": [948, 614],
    "Klenter|Wooo wooo wooooo!": [948, 614],
    "Klenter|You pathetic excuse for a thief!": [948, 614],
    "Klenter|You worm! May the Devourer take your soul!": [948, 614],
    "Possessed Priest|Yes mistress...": [11608, 13989],
    "Priest|A likely story. She would never reduce herself to talk to one as lowly as you, never mind help you!": [4207, 615],
    "Priest|Bother me not. I am preparing for the ceremony. I'm sure even you can curb your trivial demands until after that.": [4207, 616],
    "Priest|Good day, adventurer.": [4208, 588],
    "Priest|Greetings. May the blessings of Icthlarin rest on your tired shoulders and set you at ease during these strange times.": [4207, 590],
    "Priest|I'm afraid my orders are clear.": [4208, 588],
    "Priest|Sorry, but Sophanem is under quarantine. No one may leave or enter.": [4208, 589],
    "Priest|What do you want, cursed one?": [4207, 614],
    "Priest|Yes. The High Priest has given you permission to come and go as you please.": [4208, 589],
    "Raetul|Do come again.": [4204, 567],
    "Raetul|Good afternoon.": [4204, 567],
    "Raetul|It's hot and sunny, which is good enough for me. So can I help you with anything?": [4204, 555],
    "Raetul|Of course. That will be 30 coins please and thank you.": [4204, 567],
    "Sphinx|... but if you answer incorrectly, I get to keep your cat.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|A common saying about Tumeken is that you see him wherever you look, but never actually notice him.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|A husband and wife have six sons and each son has one sister. How many people are in the family?": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|A wanderer?": [4209, 554],
    "Sphinx|Ah, how interesting... a cat. Come here to me, kitty.": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|Ah, human. How go things, great guardian of cats?": [4209, 567],
    "Sphinx|Are you sure?": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|As a thank you for looking after them, Icthlarin grants me eternal life.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Cats play a significant role in the religion of this area, particularly when it comes to guarding the dead from the Devourer.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Cats play a significant role when it comes to guarding the dead from the Devourer. As such, they are great allies to Icthlarin.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Do you think that you'll be able to communicate with me at a deeper level because you're wearing that amulet of catspeak?": [4209, 556],
    "Sphinx|Elidinis is the goddess of fertility. The River Elid is named in her honour, for it brings life to the whole region.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Flattery, my adventurer, will get you everywhere. But to answer your question, Sophanem has been struck with plagues.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Here, I have a token that he will know is from me. Take that to him, and I'm sure he will speak with you.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|How disappointing. Still, nothing ventured, nothing gained. Goodbye.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|How very foolish.": [4209, 575],
    "Sphinx|However, I suggest you seek out the new High Priest of Icthlarin to the south east. He might be able to assist you. Of course, you'll need to convince him to talk to you first.": [4209, 591],
    "Sphinx|Human, your cat tells me that you are yet to speak to the High Priest. I wonder why I tried to help at all.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Humans are fickle. Perhaps they grew bored of her?": [4209, 554],
    "Sphinx|I am an agent of neither good nor evil. I am unconcerned with the plight of mankind and their petty wars and beliefs.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|I am the guardian of feline kind.": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|I can smell the rotting organs from here.": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|I don't need to mock you, human. You're doing a good enough job of that on your own.": [4209, 568],
    "Sphinx|I never said it did. I'm just saying that things are often not as straightforward as they seem, especially when it comes to Icthlarin and the Devourer.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|I thought that would be pretty obvious.": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|I'd have thought you'd be more than familiar with her by now.": [4209, 576],
    "Sphinx|I'll help you if you can solve a simple puzzle of mine, but...": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Icthlarin is the Menaphite god of the dead. By desecrating the tomb of one of his priests, you've made an enemy out of every person in this city.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Icthlarin is the god of the dead. He is the son of Tumeken and Elidinis, and brother to the Devourer. As this is the city of the dead, he's quite popular here.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Icthlarin is the god of the dead. He takes care of the passing of souls to their next life. The Devourer is the goddess of destruction, and that is what she craves.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|If you wish to know about the lesser gods, you should speak with Jex at the Temple of the Lesser Gods. I suppose I could spare a moment or two to tell you about the main four though.": [4209, 591],
    "Sphinx|In some ways. You humans sometimes say that 'you have to be cruel to be kind'. That seems a fitting way to describe Tumeken.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Indeed.": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|Interesting, very interesting. I'm afraid I do not know what happened to you, but it sounds like quite a bit occurred between you meeting that wanderer and now.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Interesting. I'm afraid I can't help you. I have my own concerns without involving myself with petty human affairs.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Is causing death enough to make one evil? Icthlarin is the god of the dead. By your argument, surely he is the most evil of them all.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|More so than many others in the pantheon, but not as much as she once was.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Not everything that destroys is evil. Destruction is often a necessity.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Nothing of the sort. As I've said before, I have no interest in humans and their gods. I look after my kind. For that, Icthlarin looks after me.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Nothing of the sort. I have no interest in the gods or their followers. Instead, Icthlarin and I have an understanding.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Or was it the Empty Lord they left him for... I forget.": [4209, 575],
    "Sphinx|Perhaps you should try to find something to remind you again. I find that important objects and locations can trigger memories, no matter how repressed they are.": [4209, 591],
    "Sphinx|Quite a number. There's a plague of frogs to the west. In the east, you can also find locusts.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Really? Because if I'm not mistaken, that's Klenter's shade right over there. He definitely doesn't seem happy with you. There's also the burial jar in your possession. How do you explain that?": [4209, 557],
    "Sphinx|Regardless, they are a race that have regularly associated themselves with gods considered evil. Interesting company for one such as Icthlarin to keep.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|She was not always called such. She is known by her deeds now, rather than her name.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|She's the very incarnation of destruction.": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|So, what do you need human?": [4209, 554],
    "Sphinx|Sophanem is called the city of the dead because the dead are brought here. Death plays a rather large role in the beliefs of the people and, as a result, the business.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|That is the common belief, but things are rarely that simple. In some ways, neither of them are good or bad.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|That's not quite what I said. Still, is destruction enough to make one evil? Fire destroys, but is that evil?": [4209, 555],
    "Sphinx|The Devourer wishes to destroy every soul in existence, living or dead. As you can imagine, this has brought her into conflict with Icthlarin.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|The burial jar?": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|The cows have only been producing sour milk since the outbreak, and the residents have been struck down by a rash of spots.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|The two main gods of the pantheon are Tumeken, the god of light, and Elidinis, the goddess of fertility.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Then I suggest you find something to remind you. I find that important objects and locations can trigger memories, no matter how repressed they are.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|There are some who even believe the river to be Elidinis herself.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Too true, you didn't rob just anybody's grave. You managed to rob the grave of Klenter, the recently deceased High Priest of Icthlarin. Do you know what that means?": [4209, 557],
    "Sphinx|Try the large building in the south west of Sophanem.": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|Tumeken and Elidinis also have two children. Icthlarin is one, and the Devourer is the other.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Tumeken is the god of light and husband to Elidinis. He is the leading god of the Menaphite Pantheon.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Very well. The Devourer is the goddess of destruction. As such, she is commonly considered an evil goddess, but this is an oversimplification.": [4209, 577],
    "Sphinx|Very well. What do you want to dicuss?": [4209, 554],
    "Sphinx|We could have an overlong theological debate now, but let's instead get to my point. Destruction has a place, so maybe the Devourer does as well. However, she has taken it too far.": [4209, 591],
    "Sphinx|We've already had this conversation, have we not? You're in a spot of bother, but you can't remember what happened to you.": [4209, 556],
    "Sphinx|Well answered, human. I guess you get to keep your cat.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Well anticipated. The Devourer is terrified of cats for reasons I will not explain. However, her followers, although few in number, are not. I ensure the survival of cats. For this service, Icthlarin grants me eternal life.": [4209, 591],
    "Sphinx|Well if you're after the human take on things, you'd be better off asking a human.": [4209, 555],
    "Sphinx|Well the Menaphite Pantheon is made up of four main deities.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|Well, I have to say I enjoy a laugh at someone's expense now and again... so let's have a bit of fun.": [4209, 568],
    "Sphinx|What understanding do you have of the Menaphite gods?": [4209, 555],
    "Sphinx|With your grave robbing problem?": [4209, 588],
    "Sphinx|Yes, your cat told me already. Something to do with grave robbing, tisk tisk. So unbecoming of a guardian of cats.": [4209, 590],
    "Sphinx|Yes, your companion tells me that you are in a spot of bother.": [4209, 589],
    "Sphinx|You clearly know little of Icthlarin and his past. Are you aware of the Mahjarrat? They once served Icthlarin, before they left him for Zamorak.": [4209, 556],
    "Wanderer|Aghhh get that cat away from me. Quickly please.": [6187, 571],
    "Wanderer|Don't blink...": [6187, 588],
    "Wanderer|First bring me some supplies and then I'll tell you. I'm running low and I'm about to embark on a long journey.": [4193, 590],
    "Wanderer|Fool! Only I can give you the knowledge on the secret passageway!": [6187, 615],
    "Wanderer|Get me a full waterskin and a tinderbox. I seem to have lost my own and these desert nights are very cold.": [4193, 589],
    "Wanderer|Get the cat away from me first and then I'll tell you.": [6187, 596],
